  "tldr": [
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "What sort of maths are LLMs good at?",
      "url": "https://gowers.wordpress.com/2026/08/12/what-sort-of-maths-are-llms-good-at/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49270022",
      "score": 205,
      "comments": 105,
      "author": "ColinWright",
      "published": "2026-08-12T10:04:25Z",
      "bullets": [
        "LLMs excel at symbolic manipulation, pattern matching, and translating word problems into code using libraries like Python or SymPy.",
        "Exact multi-digit arithmetic requires programmatic tool execution via REPLs, as autoregressive transformers struggle with token-level state tracking.",
        "High-level mathematical performance relies on pairing models with formal verifiers like Lean 4 or structured Chain-of-Thought reasoning techniques."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Mindful coding: Purpose and intention",
      "url": "https://var0.xyz/posts/mindful-coding-purpose-and-intention.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/864m3v",
      "score": 8,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "var0xyz",
      "published": "2026-08-12T12:59:17Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Write code with explicit intent, favoring clear semantics and well-defined architecture over hasty, speculative implementation or premature optimization.",
        "Prioritize understanding system constraints before modifying codebases to minimize technical debt, unnecessary abstractions, and cognitive overhead for maintainers.",
        "Apply deliberate practice to testing, code reviews, and dependency selection to ensure all software changes directly fulfill functional requirements."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "My Homelab Got Hacked - A Postmortem",
      "url": "https://phunky.cafe/my-homelab-got-hacked/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/ugkhor",
      "score": 8,
      "comments": 1,
      "author": "colindean",
      "published": "2026-08-12T15:50:16Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Exposing unauthenticated Docker sockets or raw SSH ports to the internet invites automated compromise via credential stuffing and known exploits.",
        "Eliminate port forwarding by enforcing zero-trust mesh VPNs like Tailscale or WireGuard paired with multi-factor authentication for remote access.",
        "Segment network traffic using VLANs and deploy CrowdSec or Fail2ban to automatically detect, alert, and block malicious scanning traffic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/devops",
      "category": "devops",
      "title": "An inter-mesh deployment pipeline",
      "url": "https://blog.zm.is/an-inter-mesh-deployment-pipeline/",
